{**
 * c-modal - a question the page stops to ask over everything else on it, until
 * it is answered or put away.
 *
 * It is the browser's own dialog shown as a modal, and nearly everything it
 * does comes from there: the focus is taken into it, the page behind it is
 * inert to the keyboard, the pointer and a screen reader alike, Escape closes
 * it, and closing it gives the focus back to whatever had it before. None of
 * that is written here, so none of it can go missing from here.
 *
 * It is opened by a button that names it and the command, which a caller
 * writes as a c-button with commandfor set to the dialog's id and command set
 * to show-modal. A browser with Invoker Commands does that on its own; in one
 * without them assets/dialog.ts answers the same two attributes, listening on
 * the document, so nothing is set up per dialog and one Naja draws later works
 * the same. The cross in the header is the same kind of button with the
 * command close, and so is any button in the footer that only puts the dialog
 * away.
 *
 * It is drawn closed. A dialog drawn open would be shown without being modal -
 * nothing behind it inert, no backdrop, Escape doing nothing - and there is no
 * markup that opens one as a modal.
 *
 * It is named by its heading (aria-labelledby), so a screen reader says what
 * it asks as it opens.
 *
 * Asked to be a form (dialogForm), everything in it sits inside a form with
 * method="dialog": a submit button in it closes the dialog and leaves its value
 * as the dialog's returnValue, with no script at all. A form that goes to the
 * server is an ordinary form inside the body instead.
 *
 * A click beside it does not close it. What it asks is often half filled in,
 * and a stray click would lose that; Escape and the cross are both there.
 *
 * The page under it is held still by assets/base.css, and it is drawn in the
 * browser's top layer, above every --layout-z-* layer, with no z-index of its
 * own.
 *}

{import 'close.latte'}

{define modal, string $id, string $title, bool $dialogForm = false, ?string $testId = null}
    <dialog class="c-modal" id="{$id}" aria-labelledby="{$id}-title" data-testid="{$testId}">
        <div n:tag="$dialogForm ? 'form' : 'div'" class="c-modal__frame" n:attr="method: $dialogForm ? 'dialog' : null">
            <div class="c-modal__header">
                <h2 class="c-modal__title" id="{$id}-title">{$title}</h2>

                {include close, attributes: ['commandfor' => $id, 'command' => 'close']}
            </div>

            <div class="c-modal__body">{block modalBody}{/block}</div>

            <div class="c-modal__footer" n:ifcontent>{block modalFooter}{/block}</div>
        </div>
    </dialog>
{/define}
